{
  "module": "Training: how the numbers are learned",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "training-basics",
    "title": "Parameters, training and loss",
    "summary": "What a model's parameters are, how training differs from inference, and what the loss is that training tries to lower.",
    "covers": ["parameters", "training-vs-inference", "loss"],
    "prerequisites": []
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "parameters",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A neural network is mostly a large collection of numbers. The numbers inside its matrices and vectors are its "
            },
            {
              "text": "parameters",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", also called "
            },
            {
              "text": "weights",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "When you read that a model has "
            },
            {
              "text": "70 billion parameters",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", it means the network contains 70 billion such numbers."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 9)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "learned",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Nobody types those numbers in. They are "
            },
            {
              "text": "learned",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ": they start out unhelpful, and a process called training adjusts them until the network behaves well."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The structure of the network stays the same. What changes during training is the value of each parameter."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 9, 10)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "training",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Training",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " is the process of learning the parameters. In outline, one round is:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "Run some text through the network. This is a "
              },
              {
                "text": "forward pass",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "Measure how wrong its output is."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "Adjust the parameters to make it less wrong."
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The extra pass that works out how to adjust the parameters is the "
            },
            {
              "text": "backward pass",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". It is used only in training."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 10)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "inference",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Inference",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " is using the trained network to produce output, such as answering a prompt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "During inference the parameters are "
            },
            {
              "text": "frozen",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". The network only does forward passes, and nothing about it is adjusted, however many prompts you send."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 10)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "loss",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "How does training measure how wrong the output is? With one number, the "
            },
            {
              "text": "loss",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The loss summarises how wrong the model's predictions are on some data. "
            },
            {
              "text": "Lower is better.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " A loss of zero would mean no error at all."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 11)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "the-loop",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Now the round from before can be stated exactly: run the data forward, measure the loss, adjust the parameters so the loss becomes smaller, and repeat many times."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Over many rounds the loss falls, and that is what it means for the model to be learning. How the adjusting is done is the subject of the next lesson."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 10, 11)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "What are a model's parameters (weights)?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "correct": true,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The learned numbers in the network: the entries of its matrices and vectors"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Training adjusts them and inference uses them unchanged."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The tokens in its vocabulary"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The vocabulary is the list of tokens. Parameters are numbers."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The words of the text it is given"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is the input. Parameters are part of the model itself."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The number of tokens it can read at once"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is the context window, a limit on the input."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "teaches": ["parameters", "learned"],
      "covers": ["parameters"],
      "variants": [
        {
          "prompt": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "A model 'with 70 billion parameters' contains what?"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "options": [
            {
              "correct": true,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "70 billion learned numbers"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "That is what parameters are."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
